Source: pg-agent-gate
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~), clang | clang-21 | clang-19 | clang-15, pkg-config, libssl-dev, libicu-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/Manuelreyesbravo/pg_agent_gate

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-agent-gate
Architecture: any
Depends: postgresql-PGVERSION, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Server-side SQL proposal and approval gate for agent roles
 Verify and execute SQL proposals under an agent role's own privileges,
 record attempts and optionally require human approval before commit.
 The library must be loaded before the agent's first statement using
 shared or role-level session preload. Optional bound assertions use
 the separate pg_living_assertions extension.
